arns above the cost of capital of 10.6%, but the 2pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar.","It converts 30% of revenue into free cash flow, or 9% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 3.08x.","ROE of 9% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.2x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 24pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 33.8% of revenue on R&D and 20.9% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $2.5B (9% of market cap).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 7.64)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 14.6% over 3 years and 20.1% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","At current returns, reinvesting 4% of profits supports about 0.5% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Margins are expanding (+21.5% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 103%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.3x, 0.8% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 29, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.5%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (19 sales, net $14.3M sold).","It returns 8.4% a year to shareholders (8.4% in buybacks).","Short interest is elevated at 12.7% of the float, 3.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 5,192 employees, each generates about $813K of revenue, 1.3x the Communication Services median, and revenue has grown 24.3% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $241K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.4M (2x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $170K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":62,"head":"Avoid: priced 33% above its fair value of $14.39.","pros":["FCF margin 29.